Subject: [PATCH 11103/11171] [outer-loop] Record the scored engines and the
 ledger's silent under-read

Two results from the subagent's four-axis review, recorded on main so they
survive independently of the unmerged worktree branch that produced them.

The four post-fix r11l engines are scored against 119 held-out transitions.
Engine 1, which holds 52 literal coordinate strings, predicts the next frame
exactly on 65 percent of transitions it never saw. So 'lookup table'
described its shape correctly and implied a generalization claim the numbers
refute. The best engine is the PRE-fix one, which agrees with the earlier
finding that the context repair moved the bottleneck not at all.

The supervisor refinement ledger was reading 3 of 13 run files. Its reader
could not parse the eval's per_game shape and skipped those files silently
while still producing a well-formed ledger reporting insufficient_evidence.
stagnations_unredirected_total read 0 for eight days; it is 64. CLAUDE.md
names that count as the specification for a new arm, so the signal that was
supposed to drive arm growth was the one being dropped.

Verified before recording rather than relayed: branch commits present, 34
tests green with PYTHONPATH pinned to the worktree, and one mutation proof
reproduced by hand with a byte-identical restore.

