+### 22:05Z — the four post-fix engines are SCORED, and the ledger was reading 3 of 13 files
+
+A subagent completed a four-axis review of the live agent. Its work sits on the branch
+`worktree-agent-afd77ea2887b9da58` (commits `47689d162f`, `8013ea97e7`) and is NOT merged. The
+two results below are recorded here so they survive independently of that branch.
+
+**The engines are no longer unscored.** Every archived r11l engine was scored against 119 fresh
+level-0 random-walk transitions it had never seen (`collect_transitions("r11l", n=120, seed=0)`),
+read-only over `results/arc_e3/r11l/attempts/`.
+
+| engine | bytes | exact_acc | cell_recall |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 2026-09-02 23:28, PRE-fix | 7588 | 0.672 | 0.789 |
+| 2026-09-04 02:05, post-fix engine 1 (the 52 literal deltas) | 5046 | 0.647 | 0.699 |
+| 2026-09-04 06:24, post-fix engine 2 (the RLE decoder) | 3193 | 0.345 | 0.362 |
+| 2026-09-04 07:12, post-fix engine 3 | 6428 | 0.639 | 0.684 |
+| 2026-09-04 07:49, post-fix engine 4 | 1741 | 0.008 | 0.017 |
+| 2026-09-03 tool-loop engines (7) | 151-2525 | 0.0 to 0.244 | 0.0 to 0.310 |
+
+Two readings, kept separate.
+
+First: **a lookup table is not a null model.** Engine 1 holds 52 literal coordinate strings and
+still predicts the next frame exactly on 65 percent of transitions it never saw. Calling these
+engines "lookup tables" described their SHAPE correctly and implied a generalization claim that
+the numbers refute.
+
+Second: **the best engine is the PRE-fix one.** The context-size repair did not improve engine
+quality. That agrees with the earlier finding that the repair moved the bottleneck not at all,
+now measured on the engine side as well as the channel side. No engine reaches the 1.0 the
+planning gate wants.
+
+Limits, stated: one game, one seed, 119 transitions. Engines 3 and 4 may be level-1 engines
+scored out of their distribution. These numbers are **not** in a `results/` artifact — writing
+one would have meant a subagent writing into the evidence tree. Treat them as unrecorded science
+until an experiment carries them. The regeneration recipe is
+`WorldModelVerifier(trans).score(engine)` per attempt file.
+
+**The refinement ledger was silently reading 3 of 13 run files.** Its reader could not parse the
+eval's `per_game` shape, so it skipped every file in that shape and still produced a
+well-formed ledger. Before and after, from the committed JSON on each side:
+
+| | main | branch |
+|---|---|---|
+| files read | 3 | 13 |
+| receipts | 9 | 14 |
+| redirects | 6 | 31 |
+| games | ar25, tu93 | ar25, cd82, r11l, tu93 |
+| `stagnations_unredirected_total` | 0 | 64 |
+| status | `insufficient_evidence` | `recommendation_available` |
+
+The last two rows are the point. `stagnations_unredirected_total` is the count of stalls where
+every arm had fired and the agent was still stuck, and CLAUDE.md's Generalization-Testing Floor
+names exactly that as the written specification for a NEW arm. It read 0 for eight days. It is
+64. The ledger now carries a concrete new-arm specification.
+
+This is the healthy-but-wrong shape the QA-layer discipline is named for: a guard that produced
+clean, plausible output while ignoring 10 of 13 inputs, and reported `insufficient_evidence`
+rather than `could_not_read`.
+
+**Verified independently before recording**, not taken on the subagent's word: the branch
+commits exist and the tree is clean; its 34 new tests pass in its worktree with `PYTHONPATH`
+pinned to that worktree; and one mutation proof was reproduced by hand — deleting the heartbeat
+exclusion in `scripts/eval_run_consumer_field_lint.py` turned
+`test_a_heartbeat_key_does_not_count_as_observed` RED on a real assertion, and a byte-identical
+restore (`cmp`) returned it GREEN.
+
+**OPERATOR DECISION 3 (new).** Whether to merge that branch to main. It is 2,122 insertions
+across 16 files and touches the live agent and the eval script. It is spec-anchored
+(REQ-ARC-WMTE-7010 through 7013), tested, and mutation-proven, but the subagent also attributed
+four pre-existing test failures it did not fix. Unmerged, none of the above reaches the live
+agent.
